\par\par \b \uc2  US T-bond higher in Tokyo as dollar pares losses. \b0\par\par\uc2 482 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 05:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 18 (Reuters) - U.S. Treasuries were higher at midday in Tokyo on Thursday, recouping some of the losses incurred overnight after Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell the dollar for the yen. \par \par \uc2  The market remained cautious about additional dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan (BOJ). \par \par \uc2  "Treasuries gained as the dollar rebounded from earlier lows," said a dealer at a U.S. brokerage house. \par \par \uc2  "But people are still jittery as another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could knock the dollar below 130 yen," he added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 136.35/45 yen at 0305 GMT in Tokyo, after dipping as low as 135.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  The greenback fell sharply in New York on Wednesday, after the BOJ and the New York Federal Reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the yen, which had on Tuesday weakened to 146.75 yen. \par \par \uc2  "'Flight-to-quality' interest in Treasuries is likely to dissipate, at least for now, following the joint U.S.-Japan action," said a fixed income fund manager at a U.S. firm. \par \par \uc2  "Treasuries' downside from here would depend on how aggressively dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was nervous ahead of a Japan trip by U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers. \par \par \uc2  A senior official of Japan's Finance Ministry told reporters that Summers was likely to hold talks with Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara in Tokyo later on Thursday, followed by a meeting on Friday with Finance Minister Hikaru Matsunaga. \par \par \uc2  Summers would attend a meeting in Tokyo on Saturday of deputy finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials from the Group of Seven (G7) countries and from nations that take part in the Manila framework, the official said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. international trade figures for April will be released at 0830 EDT/1230 GMT on Thursday, followed by the release of the Federal Reserve Bank of Philadelphia's June business outlook survey at 1000 EDT/1400 GMT. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the dollar/yen rate was likely to continue stealing attention away from U.S. economic data. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters forecast, on average, an April trade deficit of $13.4 billion, compared with $13.03 billion in March. \par \par \uc2  The Philadelphia Fed's survey was forecast to show a reading of 14.0, down from 17.5 in the previous report. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 30-year Treasury bond stood at 105-23/32 as of 0319 GMT, after closing down 1-6/32 at 105-15/32 in New York on Wednesday. Its yield stood at 5.72 percent. \par \par \uc2  September T-bond futures stood at 122-13/32, up 6/32 from the previous close, after moving between 122-01/32 and 122-16/32. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02r3k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
