\par\par \b \uc2  China  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  hails Japan-U.S. yen support. \b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 04:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIJING, June 18 (Reuters) - China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong on Thursday welcomed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen and said a devaluation of the Chinese yuan was not necessary, Xinhua news agency reported. \par \par \uc2  "We are glad to see that the exchange rate of the Japanese yen is picking up," Xinhua quoted Dai as telling a gathering of Asian bankers in Beijing. \par \par \uc2  Dai, governor of the People's Bank of China, also reaffirmed that China would not devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It's unnecessary to do that," he was quoted as saying. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the battered yen surged after surprise U.S.-Japanese government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets that triggered rallies in stock markets across the United States and Europe. \par \par \uc2  China's stock markets moved upward, following the surge in Hong Kong at its opening. \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Thursday, an economist at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the yen's rebound was favourable for China. \par \par \uc2  "This should be good news for China," said the economist, who declined to be identified. \par \par \uc2  "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be sustained, then I think the yen will be stabilised," she told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "If yen continues falling, the pressure on the yuan will be greater," she said. \par \par \uc2  In the days before Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , China had steadily turned up the heat on Japan and the United States to force them to halt the yen's precipitous slide, warning of mounting pressures on the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday Sun Zhenyu, the vice minister for foreign trade told Reuters in an interview: \par \par \uc2  "If the change in the exchange rate puts large pressure on foreign trade and exports, or if there is a large fall in foreign trade and exports, then I am afraid we may have to consider the question of whether to make adjustments." \par \par \uc2  Sun later denied suggesting China was mulling a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  - Beijing Newsroom (86) 10-6532-1921; Fax (86) 10-6532-4978 \par \par \uc2  - Email: beijing.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02r2s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
