\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr off low in Tokyo, but BOJ caution caps topside. \b0\par\par\uc2 621 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 05:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0318 GMT\tab      TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0300 GMT\par  USD/JPY     136.30/35\tab \tab    137.08-135.50\par  USD/DEM     1.7859/62\tab \tab    1.7873-1.7810\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, June 18 (Reuters) - The dollar was off its low \par \par \uc2  against the yen by Tokyo midday on Thursday on substantial \par \par \uc2  bargain-hunting demand, but it stayed under downward pressure \par \par \uc2  due to lingering concern over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Japan action had not been detected so far on \par \par \uc2  Thursday, but concern over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \par \par \uc2  growing should dollar/yen rally gain speed, they said. \par \par \uc2  The market was also turning cautious about building fresh postions ahead of U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers arrival in Japan later on Thursday and the Group of Seven (G7) deputies meeting scheduled on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  A senior Japanese Finance Ministry official said Summers and Japanese Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara were likely to have talks later on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "Many operators are expecting the BOJ to step in if the dollar rises rapidly. In this mood, bidders were very careful and speculators were quickly taking profits even at minor rallies," a foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve of New York and the BOJ jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight and were estimated to have spent as much as $6 billion selling dollars for yen in New York overnight. \par \par \uc2  The surprising joint effort by the U.S. and Japan hammered down the dollar by more than six yen overnight. \par \par \uc2  The downtrend carried over into the Tokyo market, with active follow-through sales dominating activity in early trade, pushing the greenback to as low as 135.50 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But such falls were short-lived as bidders, such as Japanese importers and institutional investors, aggressively scrambled for dollars around the lows, they said. \par \par \uc2  "Importers and investors, who have been waiting for the dollar to drop, aggressively bought dollars below 136 yen. But speculators were very cautious after seeing the overnight dive after the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market also remembered the effort made by the BOJ in early April when it spent a record $21 billion, or about 10 percent of its foreign reserves, although the impact was limited at that time. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto said on Thursday he was happy with the impact the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  had on the market. \par \par \uc2  Hashimoto told reporters: "I am happy with the fact that the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was appreciated by the market. But I don't want to comment on (specific \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) levels." \par \par \uc2  Japan's chief government spokesman Kanezo Muraoka said on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had welcomed the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Although Japanese officials welcomed the action, many market participants had mixed views about the outlook for the dollar/yen rate. They were now focusing on the outcome of the talks between Summers and Sakakibara, and the G7 deputies meeting on Saturday, to determine trends, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "I think the U.S. will not tolerate the dollar's advance after the overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar's gains should be capped at 140 yen now," a senior Japanese bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Other dealers, however, said the fate of the dollar now depends on how Japan solves its own problems, such as the bad loans problems and the economy. \par \par \uc2  "Japan needs to come up with a stronger effort to boost its economy and clearly present it to the world as soon as possible, otherwise the dollar will regain its uptrend again rather quickly," the foreign bank dealer said. ((Chikafumi Hodo, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02jz2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
