\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr rallies vs yen as G7 fails to tame yen bears. \b0\par\par\uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab   0600 GMT    TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     131.31/34\tab \tab 131.55-129.65\par  USD/DEM     1.8047/50\tab \tab 1.8053-1.7995\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, April 16 (Reuters) - The dollar was higher by late \par \par \uc2  Tokyo on Thursday, rising by about 1.5 yen at one point after \par \par \uc2  finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors of the Group of \par \par \uc2  Seven (G7) nations failed to reverse the market's bearish \par \par \uc2  outlook for the yen. \par \par \uc2  A sharp fall in Tokyo stocks also weighed on the Japanese \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In a communique issued after their meeting in Washington on Wednesday, the G7 nations said it was important to avoid excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation which could exacerbate large external imbalances. \par \par \uc2  They also said they supported steps taken by Japan aimed at stimulating domestic demand, reducing external imbalances and correcting the yen's excessive depreciation. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar gained sharply against the yen as the market focused on comments by U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin, who said the G7 meeting did not discuss the possibility of joint action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Asked if there might be a link between joint \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  action and Japan's efforts to stimulate its economy, Rubin said: "No." \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a trust bank said: "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was mainly focused on whether other G7 nations will show willingness to join Japan in supporting the yen. \par \par \uc2  "Speculation of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was dashed by Rubin's comments." \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, said after the meeting that the G7 communique indicated coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was possible. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said Sakakibara's comments merely fuelled the market's suspicion that a difference existed between Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their stance regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Comments by Haruhiko Kuroda, director-general of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's International Finance Bureau, failed to quell that suspicion, dealers. \par \par \uc2  Asked about a difference between the United States and Japan in interpreting the G7 statement, Kuroda said in Tokyo: "Japan and the U.S. share a common view. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda said the possibility of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  always exists, but his comments had limited impact on the market. \par \par \uc2  But the market was cautious about buying the dollar too aggressively due to speculation the Bank of Japan (BOJ) could step in to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  When the dollar suddenly dropped from around 131.30 yen to around 130.50 yen in mid-morning, some dealers speculated that the BOJ may have sold dollars. \par \par \uc2  But other dealers said the dollar's fall was caused by talk of dollar sales worth of $500-$700 million by the World Bank, probably due to redemption of bond issues. \par \par \uc2  The dollar quickly bounced back on solid buying by Japanese investors and importers. \par \par \uc2  But some dealers said the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be facing a renewed dilemma over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Solo action by the BOJ would support the market's view that other G7 members are unwilling to participate in joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to remain unwilling to conduct dollar-sales \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to concerns over the possible negative effects a weak dollar might have on New York stocks. \par \par \uc2  ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4g07b7q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
