\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr up in late Tokyo amid BOJ absence, awaits G7. \b0\par\par\uc2 658 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0610 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     130.16/21\tab \tab 130.37-129.47\par  USD/DEM     1.8225/35\tab \tab 1.8253-1.8211\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, April 14 (Reuters) - The dollar was firm against the \par \par \uc2  yen by late afternoon on Tuesday, due to active purchases by \par \par \uc2  Japanese investors and U.S. fund operators amid the absence of \par \par \uc2  the Bank of Japan, which had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market recently. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar was capped by profit-taking as the market \par \par \uc2  was cautious ahead of Wednesday's meeting of finance ministers \par \par \uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors from the Group of Seven nations. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was also lifted by buying related to the setting up of fresh investment trust funds and buy-backs by interbank players who had earlier set up short dollar positions on speculation that the BOJ might step in to sell dollars. \par \par \uc2  Speculative buying in mid-afternoon aimed at triggering stop-loss buy orders between 130 and 130.30 yen had pushed the greenback to the day's high of 130.37 yen before profit-taking emerged, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the BOJ's absence so far this week raised speculation that its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  late last week might have been only aimed at slowing the pace of the greenback's rise. \par \par \uc2  "There was a view among some participants that the BOJ's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have only be aimed at slowing down the pace of the dollar's rise. This prompted investors to buy dollars," said a senior trader at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, head of the International Finance Bureau at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF), told Reuters on Tuesday that excessive weakness of the yen was not favourable. But his remarks had limited impact on the dollar/yen rate. \par \par \uc2  He also said the G7 nations will discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at a meeting in Washington this week, adding that he believed other G7 nations felt the same way about the yen. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said they were sceptical that other G7 nations would be willing to take part in concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  "After the BOJ's aggressive dollar-sales \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Thursday and Friday, people are cautious about pushing the dollar too far above 130 yen before G7," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  "But other G7 members are more likely to give only verbal support for Japan's concerns about the weak yen and stop short of committing themselves to concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . So the dollar is likely to head higher after the G7," he added. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to be reluctant about conducting dollar-sales \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that might have potentially harmful effects on U.S. asset markets. \par \par \uc2  Prices of U.S. Treasuries dropped on Monday in New York amid talk the BOJ had sold about $12 billion of Treasury bills in order to raise cash. The New York Fed said on Monday it was conducting a "customer-related" transaction. \par \par \uc2  MOF's Kuroda declined on Tuesday to comment on this rumour. \par \par \uc2  Some Tokyo dealers said the sales of Treasury bills might have been part of the BOJ's preparations for possible future \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said they were bullish about the dollar's outlook after U.S. financial authorities last week expressed caution about higher U.S. inflation. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Federal Reserve Governor Laurence Meyer said last Thursday that U.S. economic growth needed to slow in order to reach a sustainable rate. \par \par \uc2  "Asia may accomplish this, in which case it would substitute for monetary tightening that in my judgment would otherwise be required," Meyer said on Thursday in a speech prepared for an Atlanta Fed public policy meeting. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 129.64/69 yen and 1.8235/40 marks in New York on Monday. ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4e07eg0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
