\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED-BoJ says it sold dlrs for yen, Fed sells for BoJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, April 9 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan sold dollars for yen in the New York market early Thursday and said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold dollars for yen on its behalf, a Bank of Japan official here said.(Clarifies action of U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ). \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan is about yen in the New York market only," a market official at the Bank of Japan's New York representative office said. He added the selling was conducted by "only Bank of Japan, not (the) Fed." \par \par \uc2  He later clarified his earlier remarks and said the Fed had sold on the Bank of Japan's behalf. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the morning \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said the Federal Reserve Bank of New York, which conducts \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the U.S. Treasury, had been seen selling dollars for yen on the Electronic Brokerage System. \par \par \uc2  "They have been doing it on the Electronic Brokerage System and direct and I imagine we will get a call eventually. I am surprised we haven't (yet), but people I have talked to have seen them," a senior foreign dealer at a major U.S. bank said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin welcomed Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but made no mention whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  was joining them. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen had been gaining in thinned pre-holiday trading as investors registered disappointment after Japanese Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto overnight announced a fresh 10 trillion yen stimulus package. \par \par \uc2  But then the dollar slumped abruptly in New York trading, falling as low as 129.52 yen from 133.10 at the open. Dealers said selling occurred quickly at multiple levels. \par \par \uc2  Other Group of Seven nations, including Germany and the UK, declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  The Bundesbank, in keeping with its practice to stay silent on market rumors, did not say say whether it had been involved in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  A Bank of England official said the British \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no comment to make on the developments. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the move came at the right time as it surprisedthe market and should be successful in shoring up the yen - at least temporarily. \par \par \uc2  ((-North American Treasury Desk, 212-859-1639 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4907ivl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
