\par\par \b \uc2  Ex-Fed Blinder doubts UK would join euro soon. \b0\par\par\uc2 529 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Sept 26 (Reuter) - The UK will almost certainly join the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although at a later stage than the planned 1999 euro launch, former Federal Reserve Vice Chairman Alan Blinder said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "It's extremely likely the UK would want to join eventually, but very doubtful the UK would want to join soon," Blinder told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  A Financial Times article on Friday said the British government has adopted a more favorable stance toward the European monetary union (EMU). Prime Minister Tony Blair's office, however, called the report "speculation." \par \par \uc2  "The likelihood of a timely launch for the euro is very high -- and with a large group of countries, as opposed to a small group. It's likely to include Italy, Spain and Portugal," said Blinder, a professor of economics at Princeton University, who this week joined the advisory firm G7 Group as vice chairman. \par \par \uc2  "It's fundamentally the political will in France and Germany. They seem very much on board," stressed Blinder who predicted that the new European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep a tight monetary policy to ensure the stability of the new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- at least at first. \par \par \uc2  "The emphasis will be on tight monetary and fiscal policies to meet the (economic and debt convergence) criteria. We'll see tight money in Europe for some time," the former Fed vice chairman forecast. \par \par \uc2  While Blinder acknowledged that some uncertainty remained, he did not expect the euro plan to collapse at this stage. \par \par \uc2  "Given how far Europe has come down this road, finishing the job is vastly better, both politically and economically, than letting the thing fall apart, which would be very disruptive," he said. "There is a whole history behind (the euro) and History really matters." \par \par \uc2  While Blinder expected the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be a factor of stability for Europe, he did not rule out some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility. \par \par \uc2  "The euro will start trading at the value of the ECU on the closing day of business in 1998. Versus the dollar, it's probably going to be pretty much the same as it is today. The parity within Europe has been very stable," Blinder added. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/ECU currently trades at 1.1135. \par \par \uc2  "The European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would want to establish the euro as a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it is supposed to be equipped with a lot of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves," Blinder said. \par \par \uc2  The Fed holds foreign reserves in yen and marks only. The mark reserves will be converted into euros, but it remains unclear how efficient the U.S. monetary authorities would be at defending the dollar versus the euro, if needed. \par \par \uc2  "It's a very controversial question with various answers. But it's also a mute question almost, because the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not very \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -minded and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  very infrequently and only in small mounts," added Blinder who doubted the United States' or other countries' ability to stand up to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets "to stem a very stong tide pushing in one direction or another." \par \par \uc2  The G7 Group also is the publisher of a G7 Daily Briefing. \par \par \uc2  (( Isabelle Clary, 212-859-1666 )) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dt9q01uxw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
