\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr ends flat vs mark, yen in U.S. as stg crumbles. \b0\par\par\uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, May 7 (Reuter) - The dollar closed nearly unchanged in the U.S. versus the mark and yen, but rose against sterling, which crumbled after a wire report stated an anonymous Labour Party source supports a weaker pound, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The pound fell over two cents after a Bridge News report quoted an unnamed Labour source as saying sterling should rejoin Europe's Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM) in 2001 at a rate of 2.50 marks, well below its current 2.7790 mark rate, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 125.05/10 yen versus 125.00/10 at Wednesday's open, and 1.7190/00 marks compared to 1.7195/05.z Sterling melted to $1.6150/60 from $1.6372/82. \par \par \uc2  Sterling's steep slide was proof of market nervousness over the embryonic dollar policy of the Labour Party, which ended 18-years of Conservative Party rule in last week's landslide election victory. \par \par \uc2  "The news story states that the Labour Party does in fact have a bias towards a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not wanting to hinder employment from the export side," said David Durrant, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at I.D.E.A. consultancy. \par \par \uc2  "But they also want a little tighter interest rate policy, so they are on both sides of the fence," Durrant added. \par \par \uc2  The UK raised its official interest rate 25 basis points to 6.25 percent on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shed a full yen, hitting a low of 124.60 yen, after Japan's Kyodo news agency reported an unnamed international monetary source as saying Germany, the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan were exploring the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ailing yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has risen 10 percent so far this year against the yen, reaching a 56-month high of 127.47 yen on May 1. \par \par \uc2  Dollar volatility versus the yen was exacerbated by conflicting remarks from two Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials over Japan's readiness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a surge in Japan's trade surplus. \par \par \uc2  MOF official Eisuke Sakakibara said it would be difficult to procure funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly from the money market, while another official told Reuters Japan can, if needed, use some $220 billion of external reserves. \par \par \uc2  "If the Japanese do want to go forward with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they have more than ample \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to sell dollars," said Ben Strauss, an assistant vice president at Bank Julius Baer and Co. \par \par \uc2  "Right now, I think the G3 (Group of Three) doesn't have thewill to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and frankly is not all that concerned. Currentlevels are appropriate from a fundamental economic standpoint," he added. \par \par \uc2  Japan posted a customs-cleared trade surplus of 352.67 billion yen in the first 20 days of April, a swing from a 59.06 billion deficit in the same period last year. \par \par \uc2  There was no indication outside of Japan that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was being discussed. Officials at Germany's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. Treasury declined to comment on the report. \par \par \uc2  Traders also said dollar/yen's early slip reflects diminishing prospects for a Federal Reserve rate rise at the May20 policy-setting meeting and prospects Japan may soon raise \par \par \uc2  interest rates, which currently lie at historic lows. \par \par \uc2  "The lower dollar is a factor of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the possible turning of Japanese interest rates. The dollar could keep softer versus the yen for the next couple of weeks," said Mark Gargano, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives at First Union National Bank. \par \par \uc2  Also depressing the dollar was a 140 point drop in the Dow industrials and a near full-point loss in the benchmark 30-year Treasury bond. \par \par \uc2  The release of the Federal Reserve's latest summary of economic activity, called the Beige Book, did little to change economists' U.S. interest rate outlook. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the U.S. economy expanded moderately over the past two months with wages and retail sales remaining generally subdued. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the dollar was nearly flat at 1.4581/86 Swiss francs from 1.4580/90, but rose to Canadian $1.3817/22 from C$1.3811/16. The Australian dollar ended at $0.7766/71. \par \par \uc2  ((-- Roanne Daniels, 212-859-1677)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5705zmz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
