\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr/mark ends in US above 1.73, dlr/yen shy of 127. \b0\par\par\uc2 529 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, April 28 (Reuter) - The dollar drifted higher by the U.S. close, recovering from a bout of profit-taking after the weekend Group of Seven nations meeting pushed the dollar sharply higher against the mark and yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar surged to a 37-month peak against the German mark and near its 55-month high against the Japanese yen after the outcome of Sunday's meeting between G7 officials in Washington was more lenient than traders had anticipated. \par \par \uc2  "If anything, the market was a little surprised of the lack of forcefulness in the G7 comments," said Dennis Pettit, trading manager at Long Term Credit Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the market perceives any heightened risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today as opposed to Friday," he added. \par \par \uc2  Traders said neither the official communique released after the G7 gathering nor comments by officials gave any hint that they plan to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, a measure the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not used since August 1995. \par \par \uc2  But U.S officials did publically pressure Japan to prevent a "significant increase" in its trade surplus with the rest of the world. Further weakening of the yen could widen the nation's trade surplus. \par \par \uc2  "The communique suggested it is a case of watching the pot, but it's not boiling yet," Ron Leven, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan. \par \par \uc2  "There are references to not wanting trade to become a problem without saying it is a problem," he added. \par \par \uc2  In the communique, finance ministers said major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  misalignments had been corrected, and excessive volatility and deviations from fundamentals were undesirable. \par \par \uc2  Shortly after the dollar reached its highs in the Far East, dealers began to cash in profits and pushed the U.S. unit down to just above Friday's U.S. close. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended Monday's U.S. session at 1.7320/30 marks, below its 1.7389 marks Tokyo high but above its 1.7316/19 open. Against the yen, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 126.83/88, also below its 127.08 high but above the 126.63/73 open. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's retreat against the mark was compounded by investors selling the British pound and buying marks ahead of Thursday's UK general election, which polls show will bring 18 years of unbroken Conservative Party rule to an end in favor of Tony Blair's Labor Party. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the dollar rose against its Canadian counterpart after Canada's Prime Minister Jean Chretien, on Sunday, called a June 2 general election, 17 months before the required date. \par \par \uc2  Chretien has only governed for 3-1/2 years, but currently has a broad lead in the polls over a badly split opposition. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to Canadian $1.4001/06 from C$1.3978/83. Sterling inched higher to $1.6242/52 from $1.6235/45 and the dollar rose to 1.4730/40 Swiss francs from 1.4725/35. The Australian dollar fell to $0.7800/05 from $0.7804/09. \par \par \uc2  ((-- Roanne Daniels, 212-859-1677)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4s06fo2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
