\par\par \b \uc2  Greenspan says sceptical on  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  ranges. \b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 19 (Reuter) - U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan told a news conference in Tokyo on Tuesday that he was sceptical about the concept of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ranges. \par \par \uc2  "Until I see some evidence...that such types of ranges really do work, I would be sceptical," he said. \par \par \uc2  Referring to opinions about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ranges held by financial analysts such as Fred Bergsten, he added: \par \par \uc2  "I'm less inclined to believe you can implement these kinds of ranges. \par \par \uc2  "The type of system we have probably is about as good as we are going to get for the time being." \par \par \uc2  Greenspan also said that he felt the "Big Bang" financial reform plan announced by Japan last week would contribute to the wider use of the yen as an international \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I don't see how it can fail," he said, adding that "one of the basic problems in not investing in yen-based securities is the underlying structure". \par \par \uc2  Greenspan said he had no real views on the issue of whether it was better for central banks or finance ministries to have control over \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , adding that in the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  there was "de facto collaboration" between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Treasury. \par \par \uc2  Concerning past experience of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with Japan, he said: "We have found the system works pretty seamlessly and have been quite pleased." \par \par \uc2  Japan is currently working on reform of the law governing the Bank of Japan with the aim of boosting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independence. \par \par \uc2  Greenspan arrived in Japan on Sunday for meetings with financial and monetary authorities. He was scheduled to leave later on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018dsbj00b7c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
