\par\par \b \uc2  TIETMEYER HINTS AT MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION \highlight\uc2  FOR DOLLAR. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Svea Herbst-Bayliss \par \uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  FRANKFURT, Oct 24 (Reuter) - Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said on Tuesday recent \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements were exaggerated and that the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be willing to participate in concerted market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We are willing to participate in sensible international cooperation in the future. Benign neglect was never our policy," Tietmeyer said in the text of a speech aimed at shoring up the dollar after several days in which it has been struggling against the powerful mark. \par \par \uc2  The Bundesbank last took part in concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan to boost the dollar on August 15, a move that took the markets by surprise and sent the dollar from about 1.43 marks to as high as 1.47. \par \par \uc2  The Bundesbank has always been very cautious in showing its hand about potential market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Tietmeyer's comments were unusually forthright. His words, seen as a warning to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators, came at the end of a day in which the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regained half a pfennig to 1.3865 marks. It rose further to 1.3935 marks after his comments. \par \par \uc2  Tietmeyer said temporary exaggerations can occur in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market "as is again the case at present" in the dollar's recent stumble against the mark. \par \par \uc2  He warned that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  crises can only be solved permanently if countries tackle what he called "uncertainties about political decisions taken by some of our partner nations". \par \par \uc2  Tietmeyer's remarks were echoed by Bundesbank board member Gerd Haeusler, who also said on Tuesday that coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can work in some occasions. \par \par \uc2  The Bundesbank has traditionally urged nations to solve their own internal problems to ensure keeping their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  appropriately valued. \par \par \uc2  The dollar, which recovered during the summer after a bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by several central banks, recently dropped to its lowest level in 11 weeks against the mark, falling victim again to political turmoil in Europe.With a no-confidence vote threatening Italian Prime Minister Lamberto Dini's government and fresh scandal threatening the French government, investors shunned the Italian lira and French franc in favour of marks and Swiss francs. \par \par \uc2  The mark's strength has led to economic forecasters lowering their outlooks for the German economy and has caused strong concern among export-sensitive companies. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040129drap00rhj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
