\par\par \b \uc2  Japan reproaches U.S. over dollar, urges action. \b0\par\par\uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 20 (Reuter) - Japan reproached the United States on Thursday for the dollar's plunge to record lows against the yen and urged Washington to take action, saying U.S. credibility was at stake. \par \par \uc2  In a mounting battle of words over the dollar's plight, Prime Minister Tomiichi Murayama called on the United States to tackle its trade and budget deficits to help restore the dollar's strength. \par \par \uc2  Washington has not been troubled'' by the dollar's fall as much as Japan because the U.S. economy is stable and the dollar steady against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Mexico and Canada, its major trading partners, Murayama told a parliamentary panel. \par \par \uc2  But Washington must be concerned about the dollar's decline because a weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  means a decline in America's credibility,'' he said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Finance Minister Masayoshi Takemura added his voice to the call for U.S. action, telling parliament he hoped Washington would come up with specific measures to back up its stated desire for a strong dollar. \par \par \uc2  The relentless drop in the dollar, which has fallen more than 20 percent this year to a post-World War Two low of 79.75 yen on Wednesday, has become a major source of friction between Tokyo and Washington. \par \par \uc2  Murayama conceded that the two nations were having trouble coordinating efforts on the dollar. At present, difficulties may exist between the two in cooperating,'' he said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. officials have said Japan's failure to cut its huge trade surplus is one of the main reasons for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  instability. Japan concedes this, but also points its finger at the U.S. budget and trade deficits. \par \par \uc2  The stalemate in U.S.-Japan talks on auto trade also hangs over the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, where many participants believe Washington wants a weaker dollar against the yen to force Japan to make trade concessions. \par \par \uc2  Trade minister Ryutaro Hashimoto, speaking to the same panel on Thursday, accused American car and car parts makers of not trying hard enough to crack the Japanese market. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. government is putting forward arguments (in the auto talks) while ignoring the fact that U.S. companies are not making enough efforts to do business in Japan,'' Hashimoto said. \par \par \uc2  High-level talks on car trade in Washington earlier this week failed to narrow the gap between the two sides. The United States has threatened to slap trade sanctions on Japan if the dispute is not resolved. \par \par \uc2  Japan says a such a move would prompt it to halt the talks and take the case to the Geneva-based World Trade Organisation. \par \par \uc2  The yen's appreciation against the dollar, which was trading around 81.55 yen in afternoon trade on Thursday, threatens to stifle Japan's economic recovery by slashing exporters' profits and hurting their competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Yasuo Matsushita told parliament that the current exchange rate does not reflect the economies and interest rates of the two nations. \par \par \uc2  Monetary authorities are exchanging information in order to take appropriate steps against the unstable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements,'' he said. \par \par \uc2  But he did not elaborate on what international steps might be taken. In recent months the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  has rarely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and it has not raised interest rates, a step which many economists believe is vital to defend the dollar. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr4k08ndf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
